        "community": "Taykwa Tagamou Nation",
        "communityKey": "taykwatagamounation",
        "item": "Youth support",
        "description": "Previous information: There is no specific programming for survivors within the community but at a political territorial level, there is support as well as with CSSA. Nishnawbe Aski Nation created an advisory council named The SAFE council which stands for Survivor and Family Empowerment. It is a survivor-led initiative that promotes the inclusion of survivors’ and families’ voices and provides direction for the vision of how the work by the department needs to be approached. The group utilizes their knowledge, lived experience, and expertise as survivors of residential school. \n\nRevised information: Youth support is visible through a Recreation & Youth Coordinator (Nancy Gagnon, nancy@taykwatagamou.com\n(705) 272-5766 Ext. 259), the Pathfinder program, and social-service programming intended to support childern, youth, adults, and elders. Child Wellbeing Law page also points towards care and services for children and families.",
        "date": "2026-04-07 00:00:00",
        "note": ""
