        "item": "Survivors support",
        "description": "Previous information: There is no specific programming for survivors within the community but at a political territorial level, there is support as well as with CSSA. Nishnawbe Aski Nation created an advisory council named The SAFE council which stands for Survivor and Family Empowerment. It is a survivor-led initiative that promotes the inclusion of survivors’ and families’ voices and provides direction for the vision of how the work by the department needs to be approached. The group utilizes their knowledge, lived experience, and expertise as survivors of residential school. \n\nAdditional information: Support appears to be through general health, mental health, crisis, family wellbeing, and holistic social services. Health page",
