        "item": "Youth Support",
        "description": "Previous Information:\nChild Wellbeing Law: TTN's own law prevents children from entering unfamiliar care systems, aiming to keep them within the community by providing wrap-around support, preventing separation, and focusing on family reunification.\n Child Well-Being Law | Protecting TTN Children & Families – Taykwa Tagamou Nation \n\n\nKunuwanimano Child & Family Services: Provides intake, case management, customary care coordination, and family support, working to keep children safely within the community.\nhttps://www.oacas.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/20%20-%20Kunu%20-%20Child%20and%20Youth%20Worker%20-%20Takwya.pdf#:~:text=Monitor%20youth%20progress%20and%20cultural%20needs%20%E2%80%A2,lines%20and%20provides%20written%20reports%20as%20requested.\n\nRevised Information:\nDuplicate Record",
