        "item": "Emotional Support",
        "description": "Previous information: Community Hub\n\nServices and programming: \n\nhealthy living education \ncultural programming \nland-based activities \nprevention programs \nanti-violence prevention program \nprogram that promote family unity\n healthy snack program\n\nReference\nhttps://www.missanabiecreefn.com/single-post/job-opportunity-timmins-hub-worker \n\nFamily Support \n\nServices and programming:\nAwareness/prevention programs ·\n Prevention focused programs and support groups for families of children living with different disorder spectrums.\nEducational sessions for parents that focus on the circle of security parenting and developmental milestones of children.\nSport activities and healthy living programs for children 0-6 years of age.\nPrevention services to children and their families\nSupports and advocates to Missanabie Cree families involved with any child welfare agency.\n\nReference\nhttps://www.missanabiecreefn.com/single-post/family-support-worker \n\nFamily Well-Being\n\nServices and programming:\n\nAdvocate, connect, guide, and refer families and individuals to community-based internal and external support services\nHealthy living education, e.g, teachings, diabetes education, health promotion and prevention of disease, congregate dining, etc.\nTransportation for programming\nTransportation for local medical appointment of elderly clients\nTransportation for support services (grocery trips)\nViolence prevention education and programs\nReference \nhttps://www.missanabiecreefn.com/single-post/job-posting-family-well-being-worker\n\nRevised information: The clearest community-specific support is through Family Services, especially the Family Well-Being Worker, Choose Life Coordinator, and Addictions/Mental Health Worker roles.",
