    "name": "Sagamok",
    "section": "Algoma District First Nation Communities",
    "link": "https://www.sagamokanishnawbek.com/",
    "contact": "Administration Receptionist\nTel: (705) 865-2421 | EXT : 100\n\nKristy Bennett - Administrative Assistant\nTel: (705) 865-2421 | EXT : 282\n\nAdrienne Eshkakogan - Finance Manager\nTel: (705) 865-2421 | EXT : 106\n\nDirectory",
    "physical": "The community offers Health Services through the Community Wellness Department, including Primary Care, Public Health, Medical Transportation, Foot Care, and Systems Navigation. The community also offers Home and Community Care Services through the Elders Eagle Lodge, including personal support services, homemaking, community support services, Indigenous transition support, caregiver support and respite, home maintenance, meal services, and professional services such as physiotherapy, nursing, occupational therapy, and speech-language pathology.",
    "mental": "The community offers Mental Health and Addiction services for individuals, couples, families, and groups where they can access counselling/treatment, resources, referrals, advocacy, and other supports or services that enhance wellbeing. Community also offers Counselling, Prevention and Education, Cultural Services, and Minobimaadiziwin Addiction Recovery.",
    "spiritual": "The community’s Mental Health and Addiction includes Cultural Services. The community also identifies its services as rooted in Mino-Biimaadiziwin (Living a Good Life) and says the root of services stems from the Community Story and the Comprehensive Community Plan. The community also offers gatherings and healing activities such as Community Sweatlodge Ceremony, Traditional Healing with Godfrey Shawanda, Traditional 1-on-1 Counselling Sessions, and Women’s Full Moon Ceremony.",
    "emotional": "The community offers emotional support through Mental Health and Addiction services, which are voluntary and aim to increase hope, purpose, belonging and connection among community members. A separate crisis counselling post says Sagamok provides a more accessible, culturally safe, trauma-informed, holistic crisis mental health service. he community also offers healing and wellness activities such as Traditional Healing, Women’s Retreat, and Women’s Full Moon Ceremony.",
    "survivors": "The community offers broader healing and support services through Mental Health and Addiction, Crisis Counselling, and the Child and Family Advocacy Unit. Community also offers Monthly Elder's Gatherings, Elders Forum gatherings, and related meeting space for Elders.",
    "youth": "The community offers youth support through its Education system and Youth Wellness Hub. Sagamok Anishnawbek Education Committee is an Anishnawbe, community-controlled, community-based educational network, with goals including Language and Culture, Student Success, Communication and Collaboration, and Governance and Leadership. Sagamok is working with Youth Wellness Hubs Ontario to establish a service-based youth hub in the community, and later posts invite youth ages 12–25 to help guide programs and services.",
