    "contact": "https://caodanak.com/en/contact-us/",
    "physical": "The community offers physical health services through the Centre de santé d’Odanak, including nursing clinic services, home care, prevention and information services, services for children 12 and under through “Jeunesse en santé,” and support related to physical illness prevention, screening, and home-based care.",
    "mental": "The community offers mental health services through the health centre. The Strategic Plan 2019-2024 and 2022-2023 Annual Report explicitly identify an axis to “Offrir des services en santé mentale” and describe individual mental health follow-up for adults, suicide-prevention awareness, and follow-up according to community needs.",
    "spiritual": "Community identify traditional and cultural knowledge transmission through Elders, intergenerational cultural activities, and medicinal/cultural exchange activities for Elders.",
    "emotional": "The community offers emotional support through its mental health services. Community describe interventions that take into account different spheres of a person’s life and the means available to cope with difficulties, and also identify suicide-prevention awareness and individual follow-up as part of community mental health support.\n\n2021-2022 Annual Report Snippet\n\n2022-2023 Annual Report",
    "survivors": "The community support Elders through health and home-support services, intergenerational activities, and cultural exchanges. The 2022–2023 annual report describes home nursing care and home-support services, and 2024-2025 annual reporting mentions medicinal and cultural exchange activities for Elders. Community publications also show Elders participating in intergenerational knowledge-sharing and exchanges.",
    "youth": "The community supports youth through health and education services. The community health policy includes Jeunesse en santé for children 12 and under, and the strategic plan includes a priority to update and expand education services. Community publications also show intergenerational youth activities, including a gathering where youth and Elders met for a weekend of exchanges and activities.",
    "connect": "The community offers intergenerational connection spaces through activities where youth and Elders gather together for exchanges and activities. Community publications describe a first gathering between youth and Elders, and other bulletins show Elders meeting with youth from another Nation to exchange and share. These official materials support an intergenerational connection approach based on cultural exchange and shared activities.\n\nWinter 2019 community paper\n\nSeptember 2017 community paper",
