    "link": "https://kahnawake.com",
    "contact": "https://kahnawake.com/contact-us/",
    "physical": "The community offers Home and Community Care Services, Environmental Health Services, Assisted Living Services, Turtle Bay – Elders’ Lodge, and Parenting Services through Kahnawà:ke Shakotiia’takéhnhas Community Services. KSCS Home and Community Care Services support the independence and quality of life at home for adult and elderly Kahnawa’kehró:non, and Assisted Living Services enhance the lives of community members with special needs and/or mental illnesses.",
    "mental": "The community offers Mental Wellness and Addictions, Addictions Response Services, Prevention, Youth Protection & YCJA Services, Foster Care, and Post Majority Support Services through Kahnawà:ke Shakotiia’takéhnhas Community Services. These services support community members in their journey to healing and improving wellbeing, provide compassionate support for substance use and addictions, promote mental health, address family violence, support children and youth safety and well-being, and support youth aged 16 to 25 who have aged out of foster care.",
    "spiritual": "The community offers Traditional Services through Kahnawà:ke Shakotiia’takéhnhas Community Services, including individual counselling and group healing through Tsi Niionkwarihò:ten, or “our ways.” The community also offers the Tsi Niionkwarihò:ten Tsitewaháhara'n Language and Culture Training Program, which was established to promote Kanien’kéha language and cultural education and includes both language and cultural instruction. These services fill gaps in cultural connection, traditional healing, and language/culture revitalization.",
    "emotional": "The community offers emotional support through Mental Wellness and Addictions, Addictions Response Services, Prevention, Parenting Services, and Traditional Services. These services support healing and wellbeing, provide support and resources for substance use and addictions, strengthen families, address family violence, and build a caring, connected community grounded in peace, respect, and responsibility.",
    "survivors": "The community offers broader healing and support through Traditional Services including Indian Residential School Health support, Mental Wellness and Addictions, Addictions Response Services, Prevention, Home and Community Care Services, and Turtle Bay – Elders’ Lodge.",
    "youth": "The community offers youth support through Sports & Recreation Unit, Youth Protection & YCJA Services, Foster Care, Post Majority Support Services, Prevention, and Parenting Services through Kahnawà:ke Shakotiia’takéhnhas Community Services. KSCS says Youth Protection & YCJA Services support children and youth safety and well-being while working in partnership with families, and Post Majority Support Services support youth aged 16 to 25 who have aged out of foster care.",
    "connect": "Community offers spaces for Elders, youth, and language/culture supports through the Youth Center, Elder-related supports, and language/culture programming.",
    "population": "11944",
    "populationNote": "Total Registered population as of April, 2026 - 11,944\nGovernment of Canada",
