    "section": "East",
    "link": "https://www.srmt-nsn.gov",
    "contact": "Stephanie Cook - Director of Education\nPhone: 518-358-9721\nEmail: education@srmt-nsn.gov\n\nRebecca Smoke - Youth Services Manager\nEmail: education@srmt-nsn.gov\n\nJamie Ross - Intake Coordinator\nEmail: education@srmt-nsn.gov\n\nhttps://www.srmt-nsn.gov/support-services/communications",
    "physical": "The community offers physical health services through St. Regis Mohawk Health Services, including medical clinic services, dental services, diabetes prevention and management, maternal and child health programs, environmental health, and community health outreach. These services support disease prevention, primary care access, and long-term health management for children, adults, and Elders.",
    "mental": "Kanikonri:ihne / Good Mind Counseling provides confidential outpatient mental health services for children and adults, including screening, therapy, psychiatric evaluation, crisis intervention, medication therapy, case management, parent advocacy, traditional Mohawk services, respite, home-based mental health services, wraparound services, Head Start consultation, and school-based mental health. This fills gaps in counselling, crisis support, child/youth mental health, family conflict, trauma, grief, abuse, anxiety, depression, and school-based mental health access.",
    "spiritual": "Traditional Mohawk Services are included within Mental Health Services, allowing community members to include traditional healing practices as part of their wellness journey. Health Services also frames its mission as “Body, Mind & Spirit in Harmony with our Environment.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support is provided through Good Mind Counseling, crisis intervention, family/couples/play therapy, case management, respite, home-based supports, and the Office of the Family Advocate for families in crisis or trauma who need help navigating services",
    "survivors": "Survivors are honoured through Every Child Matters / Orange Shirt Day gatherings, remembrance, ceremony, cultural pride, and community healing, and can also access support through SRMT Mental Health - Good Mind Counseling, the SRMT After Hours Crisis Center, and the National Residential School Crisis Line.",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Youth Educational Services, including corrective studies, tutoring, enrichment, physical education, summer youth programming, college visits, field trips, academic incentives, cultural activities, and career/college development. Youth mental health support is also available through Good Mind Counseling and school-based mental health services",
    "connect": "Youth and Survivors can be connected through cultural activity workshops, Kanien’keha language learning, and intergenerational knowledge-sharing programs that bring Akwesasne youth and Elders together to share traditional activities, language, and culture.",
