    "contact": "Administration\nSHECAPIO Titus - Director General\nPhone: (418)923-3461 | EXT 208\nEmail: directorgeneral@mistissini.ca\n\nHuman Resources Department\nNEEPOSH Andrew - Director of Human Resources\nPhone: (418)923-3461 | EXT 217\nEmail: aneeposh@mistissini.ca\n\nFinance Department\nBEAUDOIN Marc-Andre - Controller\nPhone: (418)923-3461 | EXT 309\nEmail: mabeaudoin@mistissini.ca\n\nStaff Directory",
    "physical": "Cree Nation of Mistissini supports members through its Health and Social Development Department by providing community-based wellness, while additional health services available in the community are provided through the Cree Health Board.",
    "mental": "Members in Cree Nation of Mistissini are supported through mental health and wellness-related services in the community, including supports connected to the Health and Social Development structure and additional services provided through the Cree Health Board.",
    "spiritual": "Members in Cree Nation of Mistissini are supported spiritually through community-based cultural, language, and elder-led supports. Community describe Eelders as holders of traditional knowledge connected to the land, Cree language, values, and wisdom, and say elders teach and guide youth. The community also has Cultural Programs & Development, Cree Language, and an Elders Council within its Health and Social Development structure. These supports help fill gaps by strengthening cultural continuity, traditional knowledge sharing, language, identity, guidance, and connection to the land.",
    "emotional": "Members in Cree Nation of Mistissini are supported emotionally through local wellness, social, cultural, elders, youth, and recreation supports available in the community.",
    "survivors": "Elders are supported through the Department of Social and Cultural Development, including free snow removal, free firewood, and transport services for elders.",
    "youth": "Youth in Cree Nation of Mistissini are supported through the Mistissini Youth Council and Youth Department, which provide dozens of programs each year supporting youth health, wellness, and development. Supports include summer, part-time, and student work experience programs; the canoe brigade, journey of wellness, and other excursions and land access activities; fitness challenges, inter-band games, and events that promote active living, art, and culture; and youth centre opportunities to learn new skills, along with local Youth Achievement Awards.",
    "connect": "Survivors and youth can be connected through Elders’ guidance, cultural teaching, and youth programs that promote Cree identity, culture, heritage, language, values, customs, traditions, and beliefs, alongside land-based and community activities organized for youth.",
