    "contact": "General Administration\nMelissa Sunday - Reception, Admin Building\nEmail: sundaym@chimnissing.ca\n\nAdministration\nHannah Jamieson - Executive Assistant\nEmail: hjamieson@chimnissing.ca\n\nFinance\nJustin Cotter - Finance Director / Manager\nEmail: financemgr@chimnissing.ca\n\nEducation\nLynda Hoksbergen - Education Director\nEmail: lynda.hoksbergen@chimnissing.ca\n\nDirectory",
    "physical": "Beausoleil First Nation provides physical health supports through Beausoleil Family Health, including the Beausoleil Family Health Centre, Medical Transportation, Oral Health, Community Health, Healthy Babies and Healthy Children, Home and Community Care, Home Support, Telemedicine, Dental Clinic, Community Health Representative/Community Health Nurse supports, and related community wellness services. Beausoleil also provides Recreation and C.A.R.E. programming, which supports physical activity, healthy development, disease prevention, obesity prevention, and overall health and wellness for members. These services help fill gaps in local health care access, transportation to medical appointments, oral/dental care, maternal and child health, elder/home support, preventative health, and active living within the community.",
    "mental": "Beausoleil First Nation provides mental health programming through Beausoleil-linked health and social service supports. It identify Mental Health, NNADAP, and Addictions/Hope and Healing as part of the community’s service areas, and Beausoleil Family Wellbeing is listed as a community department/service. Jordan’s Principle Navigator also helps families address barriers and apply for supports for children, including mental health, cultural supports, special education, recreational therapy, and related needs. These services help fill gaps in local mental wellness support, addictions support, children’s mental health access, family navigation, prevention, and connection to culturally relevant care.",
    "spiritual": "Beausoleil First Nation’s C.A.R.E. Fund provides “Cultural Education, Artistic, Recreational, and Entertainment opportunities” to members. The Recreation and Events page states that these activities promote “healthy wellness” and “healthy development,” and give members opportunities to “have fun, socialize, promote physical activity and participate in cultural activities.” The page also states that the purpose of the fund is aimed at “preventing disease, obesity and promoting overall health and wellness.”",
    "emotional": "There is a family service in place which supports families who are struggling https://chimnissing.ca/famserv.html",
