    "name": "Sucker Creek First Nation",
    "section": "West",
    "link": "https://scfn.ca/",
    "contact": "https://scfn.ca/contact/",
    "physical": "Sucker Creek First Nation delivers several health programs, including the Aboriginal Head Start On-Reserve (AHSOR) program and an Assisted Living (AL) program, managed by the community's Health and Social Development departments.\nSocial Development | Sucker Creek First Nation",
    "mental": "-Programs are designed to be culturally appropriate, non-judgmental, and trauma-informed, providing a safe space for community members to address mental health and addiction concerns.\nSucker Creek First Nation |",
    "spiritual": "Sucker Creek First Nation provides spiritual and cultural support primarily through culture-based wellness initiatives and by incorporating traditional elements into its health and social programs. \nSucker Creek First Nation |",
    "emotional": "Sucker Creek First Nation |",
    "survivors": "\"Reclaiming Our Identity\" initiative is a transformative program designed to address the lasting impacts of residential schools by fostering healing and cultural reconnection\nSucker Creek First Nation - Future Generations Foundation\n\nThe community has also dedicated a Residential School Survivors' Memorial to honor survivors and acknowledge the legacy of the schools. \nSchool survivors honoured in Sucker Creek - South Peace News",
    "youth": "Programs like the \"Reclaiming Our Identity\" initiative are effective at connecting youth with their heritage, fostering a strong sense of pride, identity, and resilience through cultural practices. This also provides a safe space for healing from intergenerational trauma.\nSucker Creek First Nation - Future Generations Foundation",
    "connect": "The \"Reclaiming Our Identity\" program\nSucker Creek First Nation - Future Generations Foundation\n\n-https://fgfoundation.ca/story-type/organization-en/",
