    "link": "http://www.yffn.ca/",
    "contact": "YFFN Band Office",
    "physical": "- Infrastructure Development: A significant development is the ongoing project to construct a new Prevention Centre adjacent to the existing hockey arena. This centre will include a gymnasium/community space and recreational spaces, directly supporting physical health and wellness activities within the community.\n\n\n-Specialized Clinics: The community has a nurse-run health office that offers a diabetes clinic and foot care, addressing specific chronic disease needs.\n\nHealth - York Factory First Nation\nYork Factory Prevention Centre",
    "mental": "Organizations like the Keewatin Tribal Council (KTC), which represents York Factory First Nation, have mental wellness teams and dedicated crisis lines that provide accessible support and connection to other services.\nMedical and Referral Transportation | Keewatin Tribal Council",
    "spiritual": "",
    "emotional": "-There is a focus on training provincial and federal staff in Indigenous-led approaches and cultural healing strategies to ensure services are culturally safe and effective.\nFirst Nations Mental Wellness Continuum Framework",
    "survivors": "access to Elders and traditional healers, ceremonies, prayers, and land-based healing activities.\nEmotional and Peer Support: Local Indigenous organizations provide access to trained, trauma-informed Indigenous health workers, peer support, dialogue, and resources to help manage emotional triggers.\nYork Factory First Nation | Aboriginal Healing Foundation",
    "youth": "",
