    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through the community’s Esiniiwab Health Centre, with named community programs including Medical Transportation Program, Healthy Babies & Healthy Children / Early Learning Program, and Community Wellness / Long-term Care",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through National Native Alcohol and Drug Abuse Program (NNADAP), which offers one-on-one counselling, group counselling, treatment referrals, aftercare, prevention and education, and cultural supports, and youth mental health is further supported through community-promoted school partnerships and services such as NorthWest Ontario Counselling & Consulting – Supporting Youth Mental Health, Supporting Youth Mental Health in Our Local Schools, and Pegamigaabo School partnerships through which students may receive mental health counselling.",
    "spiritual": "Big Grassy River First Nation supports members through the National Native Alcohol and Drug Abuse Program (NNADAP), which provides culturally grounded prevention, intervention, and referral services, is Guided by Anishinaabe values, and works with Elders, health professionals, and community partners to foster healing, resilience; through Pegamigaabo School, which supports students’ spiritual growth and well-being; through the Elders Advisory Council; and through Esiniiwab Health Centre, which will Promote prevention, education, and lifelong learning.",
