    "physical": "Anishinaabeg of Naongashiing Community Health Center provides health support that include Brighter Futures, the Community Health Representative (CHR) program, Community Wellness, Medical Transportation, and Healthy Babies and Healthy Children (HBHC), with HBHC providing support during pregnancy and for families with children from birth to school entry, including screening, home visiting, parenting support, and referrals.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through the Nation’s Health Department and Big Island Community Care Program, including Brighter Futures with a named Mental Health component, the community specifically states that the Family Counsellor/Support Worker helps by booking assessments with psychologists and therapists, making referrals for requested services, and helping ensure services are met for clients and community members.",
    "spiritual": "Spiritual and culturally grounded support is provided through National Native Alcohol and Drug Abuse Program (NNADAP), which includes traditional, spiritual and cultural programs.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support is provided through the Family Counsellor/Family Support Worker, Family Well Being Worker, Family Preservation, Community Wellness, and Brighter Futures programming, which help fill gaps in family support, parenting support, prevention, coping support, and community-based wellness.",
    "survivors": "Survivors are supported through the Ride Program for Elders, Family Counsellor/Family Support Worker, Family Well Being Worker, Mental Health Workers, Family Preservation, Community Wellness, NNADAP, and the Cultural Coordinator, which provide transportation, counselling, family support, support groups, crisis intervention, outreach, referrals, and culturally grounded support.",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Brighter Futures components such as Mental Health, Child Development, Parenting, and Healthy Babies, through the Education Department, and through Community Care roles including Alternative Care Coordinator, Child in Care Workers, Band Representative, Post Majority Support Worker, and Mental Health Workers, which together support children, youth, and families across education, care, advocacy, and wellness.",
    "connect": "Survivors and youth can be connected through the Nation’s Recreation/Community Center, which plans social, recreational, and special events for community members, alongside Community Care, Brighter Futures, Community Wellness, Family Well Being, and Cultural Coordinator supports.",
