    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through Kitchenuhmaykoosib Minoyawin Services (KMS), including Public Health Nurse, Health Planning, Home and Community Care, Medical Transportation, X-Ray, Vision Care, Community Oral Health, and Tuberculosis and HIV/AIDS prevention and education, which help fill gaps in primary care, home care, diagnostics, transport, oral health, vision care, and prevention.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through Kitchenuhmaykoosib Minoyawin Services (KMS) Mental Wellness supports, including Suicide Prevention, Mental Wellness Programs, Opioid Agonist Treatment (OAT), Suboxone, Prescription Drug Abuse Support, and Home Support, as well as NNADAP (National Native Alcohol and Drug Abuse Program) and Problem Gambling Support, which help fill gaps in counselling, crisis response, addictions care, recovery support, and ongoing mental wellness.",
    "spiritual": "Spiritual support is provided through KI’s health approach, which says KMS supports the physical, mental, emotional, and spiritual wellbeing of community members and grounds care in community values and holistic wellness, while the Choose Life Program also reconnects youth and families with nature, culture, identity, knowledge keepers, and traditional land-based skills.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support is provided through KMS, Kitchenuhmaykoosib Inninuwug Dibenjikewin Onaakonikewin (KIDO), and KI Equaygamik (Women’s Shelter), including mental wellness programs, home support, family healing, emotional support, culturally appropriate programs and services, and safe spaces for women, children, youth, and families experiencing crisis.",
