    "name": "Brunswick House First Nation",
    "section": "North",
    "link": "https://bhfn.ca/",
    "contact": "https://bhfn.ca/contact-us/",
    "physical": "-The Brunswick House Health Centre:The Brunswick House Health Centre opened its doors in February 2010.This center offers services to the band membership in areas of medical transportation, alcohol and substance abuse, counselling referrals, young mothers, diabetes clinics and elder’s assistance. \nHealth | BHFN \n\n-NIHB Program:is a national program which is designed to support First Nations people in reaching an overall health status that is comparable with Canadians.\nhttps://bhfn.ca/services/health/#:~:text=CRISIS%20TEAM-,NIHB%20PROGRAM,-The%20NIHB%20Program",
    "mental": "-Brunswick House Health Centre: Offers counselling along with a wide range of services",
    "spiritual": "Sign-Up for Smudge Kits | BHFN \nTraditional Health - Maamwesying \n\nSmudge Kits: Offering kits to on and off-reserve members to support cultural connection and spiritual wellness.\nFamily Well-Being Program: Coordinates activities like community feasts, family circles, and traditional land-based healing.\nLanguage Revitalization: Efforts to bring back and strengthen the Native language along side activities led by elders and traditional healers",
    "emotional": "-Brunswick House Health Centre: Offers counselling along with a wide range of services\nCrisis Team: Provides 24/7 intervention for family violence, immediate assistance, advocacy, and connections to safety resources, accessible via the Band Office.\nHealth | BHFN",
    "survivors": "-Brunswick House has an Elder’s Complex for independent living and has weekly programming/activities with the elder’s including:\nMeals on Wheels, Bingo’s, and Outings.\nHomecare Worker assists the elder’s with light housekeeping, and grocery shopping.\nElders | BHFN",
    "youth": "-Youth Centre/Activities/Programs\nYouth | BHFN",
