    "contact": "Cat Lake First Nation - Band Office - northwesthealthline.ca",
    "physical": "The community's nursing station (currently in temporary facilities after a fire) provides essential services, including pre-natal and post-natal home visits, home visits for the sick and elderly, and coordination of medical travel\n Cat Lake First Nation - Margaret Gray Nursing Station - northwesthealthline.ca \n\n-Brighter Future program\nCat Lake First Nation - Cat Lake Health Authority - Brighter Futures Program - northwesthealthline.ca",
    "mental": "-The Choose Life program:The \"Choose Life\" program offers culturally relevant, land-based activities to promote the mental and emotional well-being of youth, with reports of increased youth confidence and engagement.\nCat Lake First Nation - Cat Lake Wellness Centre - northwesthealthline.ca \n\n-Hope for Wellness Helpline\nHope for Wellness Helpline",
    "spiritual": "-The Cat Lake Wellness Centre\nCat Lake First Nation - Cat Lake Wellness Centre - northwesthealthline.ca",
    "emotional": "-The Choose Life program:The \"Choose Life\" program offers culturally relevant, land-based activities to promote the mental and emotional well-being of youth, with reports of increased youth confidence and engagement.\nCat Lake First Nation - Cat Lake Wellness Centre - northwesthealthline.ca",
    "survivors": "Cat Lake First Nation supports survivors through a variety of culturally grounded, community-led health and family well-being programs, complemented by national Indigenous health services",
    "youth": "-Choose Life Program:Offers land-based activities and programming promoting mental, emotional, and behavioral health for ages 0-18, funded by Nishnawbe-Aski Nation (NAN).\nFamily Well Being/Hurt & Healing Programs: Provide culturally-safe, art-based mental health support, addressing trauma, addiction, and legacy of residential schools through counselling, family circles, and traditional healing.\nOshkeemekana Treatment Centre: A residential facility for NAN youth (12-15) with addictions, offering clinical care, life skills, counseling, and traditional land-based healing.\nBrighter Futures: Runs a youth drop-in center, hosts sports, and teaches healthy living. \nCat Lake First Nation - Oshkeemekana Residential Treatment Centre - northwesthealthline.ca\nhttps://ocaarchives.files.wordpress.com/2019/01/foh-report.pdf",
    "connect": "Programs like \"Choose Life\", and traditional activities (snaring, camping) connect youth with Elders and the land for holistic well-being, contrasting with institutional settings.\nCHOOSE LIFE | Cat Lake First Nation | ᐱᔑᐎᓴᑲᐃ ᑲᓂᒃ",
