    "physical": "Community-Driven Health Planning: A successful Comprehensive Community Health Plan was developed through extensive community engagement. This ensures all health actions are guided by local principles and prioritize cultural healing, land-based skills, and supporting youth to build self-confidence and health. Infrastructure for Activity: The community has been supported in building a community centre with a gym, providing a safe, accessible space for youth activities, sports, and services like prenatal nutrition.\nPikangikum Health Authority",
    "mental": "The Pikangikum Health Authority: Promotes the development of good mental health and provides services for individuals with mental health issues\n\nMental Health & Addictions",
    "spiritual": "Pikangikum's spiritual support focuses on land-based healing, cultural practices, and suicide prevention through programs like \"Choose Life & Land-Based Healing,\"\nhttps://www.pikangikumhealth.ca/mental-wellness/choose-life-land-based-healing \n\nOur Healing Journey - Pikangikum First Nation's",
    "emotional": "Programs & Services | Pikangikum Health Authority – Comprehensive First Nations Healthcare",
    "survivors": "Safe Housing: A new safe house and hotel facility has been built to ensure that women and children in crisis have a secure place to go during an emergency.\nThe Dawsons Creating Hope in Pikangikum | Rotary Club of Norfolk Sunrise \n\nElders' Complex: The community celebrated the opening of a Knowledge Keepers Elders' Complex, providing a supportive living environment that prioritizes cultural activities and social engagement to combat isolation. \nPikangikum First Nation recently celebrated the opening of their new Knowledge Keepers Elders’ Complex. Elders can continue living in the community close to family and friends, participate in culturally relevant services, and enjoy a comfortable environment that reflects their individual needs. Image courtesy of Nik Rave Photography.",
    "youth": "Youth Hub: A central place for activities and programs promoting holistic development, honoring culture, and providing a safe space, supported by the Pikangikum Health Authority.\nYouth Hub Activities & Programs\n\nProject Journey: Uses activity-based learning, mentorship (police, elders, mentors), sports (Police Athletic League), arts, and culture to foster positive decision-making and reduce high-risk behaviors.\nView of Projects “Journey” and “Sunset” build connections for positive community impact \n\nProject Journey Enacts Positive Change in Pikangikum First Nation | SAY Magazine\n\nFamily & Community Focus: Programs emphasize family well-being, community service, and connecting youth with elders, police, and community members to build strong support networks.\n\n\nHealth & Wellness: Access to mental health services, crisis intervention, family healing centers, and addiction support are crucial components. \nChildren as young as six sniffing gas in Pikangikum - PMC",
