    "name": "Mamaweswen",
    "section": "Indigenous Health Authorities",
    "link": "https://mamaweswen.com/",
    "contact": "https://mamaweswen.com/our-administration/",
    "physical": "Education, Emergency Management,  ISETP/FNLMS- Employment and Training, Koognaasewin- Child Well-being Law, Niigaaniin-Social Services, Robinson Huron Waawiindamaagewin- Treaty Body,",
    "mental": "HART Hubs Initiative: A partnership (including Sault Ste. Marie and Blind River) to provide comprehensive services, including transitional beds and mental health supportive housing\n. Homeless and Addiction Recovery Treatment Hubs (HART Hubs): Reference Document, January 2025 | ontario.ca \n\nMinobimaadizing Addiction Services: Offers an addiction withdrawal clinic, immediate treatment options, and after-care programming.\nMinobimaadizing Addiction Services - Maamwesying \n\nMental Wellness Counselling\nMaamwesying North Shore Community Health Services - Mental Wellness and Minobimaadizing Program \n\nMental Health for Children and Yout - connect.northeasthealthline.ca \n\nCrisis Counselling - Maamwesying",
    "spiritual": "Supporting One’s Journey into the Spirit World - \n Supporting One's Journey into the Spirit World - First Nations, Inuit, & Métis (FNIM) Program - SE Health \n\nHealth Services | Mississauga First Nation \nTraditional Healing & Elders: Access to traditional healers and Elders for spiritual guidance, counseling, and traditional practices to support individual and community wellness.",
    "emotional": "Niigaaniin- Social Services",
    "survivors": "Mamaweswen North Shore Tribal Council - Cutler - N'Mninoeyaa Aboriginal Health Access Centre - Mental Health and Addiction - northeasthealthline.ca  \n\nCrisis Counselling - Maamwesying \n\nTrauma-Informed Counselling\nThe N'Mninoeyaa Aboriginal Health Access Centre (AHAC) provides specialized therapeutic support for Sexual Abuse & Family Violence: Dedicated counselling to address the immediate and long-term impacts of abuse.\nCrisis Support: Same-day, one-on-one \"Single Session Counselling\" is available with no appointment required, and PTSD Treatment: Contemporary clinical therapies, including Ontario Structured Psychotherapy, are adapted for Indigenous clients. \n\n\nResidential School & Intergenerational Support\nMamaweswen coordinates with regional partners to support survivors of the Indian Residential School (IRS) system:\nCultural & Emotional Support: Access to Traditional Healers and Elders who lead ceremonies, prayers, and dialogue for survivors and their families.\nResolution Health Support: Eligible former students and their families can access the Indian Residential Schools Resolution Health Support Program through Maamwesying referrals.\nCrisis Lines: Immediate emotional support is available 24/7 via the National Indian Residential School Crisis Line at 1-866-925-4419.",
    "youth": "ISETP Programs And Services - Mamaweswen \n\nHealth and Wellness - Maamwesying \n\nCrisis Counselling - Maamwesying- youth have access to Crisis Counselling via the central intake line (1-844-864-0523), and the organization advocates for culturally responsive supports within elementary and secondary school systems.",
    "connect": "Research link source:\nMaamwesying, North Shore Community Health Services Inc. - Mamaweswen \n\nWhitefish River First Nation\n\nZa-geh-do-win Information Clearinghouse \n\n\n\n\n\nMaamwesying North Shore Community Health Services: Provides mental health and traditional healing services across 11 First Nations, allowing for Elder-youth connection and intergenerational trauma support. \n\nZa-geh-do-win Information Clearinghouse: A central resource for research and information on family healing, supporting programs that address intergenerational trauma. \n\nSupport for Youth Mental Health & Trauma: Utilizing resources like the First Nations and Inuit Hope for Wellness Help Line and specific youth-focused mental health initiatives to foster healing.\n\nCultural Arts and Wellness Workshops: Organizing workshops focused on traditional arts, drumming, or language, allowing for natural, supportive conversation and connection. \n\nIntergenerational Mentorship Programs: Modeled after community programs that use mentorship to help youth gain leadership skills while maintaining ties to their community and history.",
    "population": "",
    "populationNote": "",
    "additionalLinks": "Niigaaniin Social Services: The Niigaaniin website details programs for financial assistance, life skills (Mino-Bimaadizidaa), and local Miijim Gaamig (Food Bank) hours. - Niigaaniin \n\nMamaweswen North Shore Tribal Council - Cutler - N'Mninoeyaa Aboriginal Health Access Centre - Mental Health and Addiction - northeasthealthline.ca\n\nMaamwesying, North Shore Community Health Services Inc. - Mamaweswen",
