    "physical": "Missing Information",
    "mental": "ACCESS Open Minds / Esprits Ouverts supports young people ages 11–25 through a youth mental health model. The model focuses on early identification, rapid access, appropriate care, continuity of care, and youth and family/carer engagement. The Early Identification guide explains that early identification is meant to raise awareness of mental health issues, reduce stigma, and help youth get support earlier. These supports help fill gaps in timely youth mental health access, early support, youth-friendly care, service navigation, continuity between youth and adult services, and family involvement.",
    "spiritual": "Missing Information",
    "emotional": "Missing Information",
    "survivors": "Missing Information",
    "youth": "ACCESS Open Minds / Esprits Ouverts supports young people ages 11–25 and their families/carers through youth mental health service sites that provide quick and easy access to support. The model includes early identification, rapid access, appropriate care, continuity of care beyond age 18, and youth and family/carer engagement, where youth and families are partners in care and service design. These supports help fill gaps in youth-friendly mental health access, early help-seeking, service navigation, family involvement, age-based service cut-offs, and timely connection to appropriate care",
